{"id":"50974324-5251-4a0f-8492-1b467ec9ea55","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"e092e916a43cd164","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/capability-calls.ts","baseline":{"blob":"6d976aaab01499ea7664f45586e2735fd903694f","start":6573,"end":6936},"shape":{"type":"For","atoms":["for","(","const","hit","of","classifyCall","(","node",",","[","]",")",")","{","const","argNode","=","node",".","arguments","[","hit",".","argIndex","]",";","const","resource","=","argNode","!==","undefined","&&","ts",".","isStringLiteralLike","(","argNode",")","?","argNode",".","text",":","\"","","\"",";","if","(","shouldBreak","(","policy",",","{","...","hit",",","\"","resource","\"",":","resource","}",")",")","{","lines",".","add","(","sourceFile",".","getLineAndCharacterOfPosition","(","node",".","getStart","(","sourceFile",")",")",".","line","+","1",")",";","}","}"]},"context":{"before":"c1f68db4ab5e56bc","after":"6b91f2256e4fbe55"}},"payload":{"text":"(no runtime args at arm time — resource comes from a literal below)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:38.131Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:38.131Z"}
{"id":"8d629a3f-fa18-4ff3-a95f-91a07ee77ba0","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"9b36e1f65f0a3541","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/capability-calls.ts","baseline":{"blob":"7397c82c638ca506647f7a7b187282b595543d4b","start":2009,"end":2023},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","arg","\"",":","number",";"]},"context":{"before":"8131ee7f8f9f05e8#1","after":"b692167e069946ac"}},"payload":{"text":"Which argument carries the resource (URL / path / command).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:48.575Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:48.575Z"}
{"id":"b724f750-9780-4c0e-a4fb-b59c73c84773","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"5c3d0596fdedba4b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/capability-calls.ts","baseline":{"blob":"385e52ff978371835891cb00901b124d1a5cb909","start":4142,"end":4584},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","classifyCall","(","node",":","ts",".","CallExpression",",","args",":","readonly","unknown","[]",")",":","CapabilityHit","[]","{","return","(","matchersFor","(","node",".","expression",")","??","[","]",")",".","map","(","(","matcher",")","=>","{","const","resource","=","args","[","matcher",".","arg","]",";","return","{","\"","capability","\"",":","matcher",".","capability",",","\"","resource","\"",":","typeof","resource","===","\"","string","\"","?","resource",":","\"","","\"",",","\"","callee","\"",":","renderCallee","(","node",".","expression",")",",","\"","dangerous","\"",":","isDangerous","(","matcher",".","capability",")",",","\"","argIndex","\"",":","matcher",".","arg","}",";","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"64ec46e7f0c20178","after":"85b27560343408eb"}},"payload":{"text":"Classify a host call at runtime into its capability hits (with the evaluated resources) — one per path a copy or a\nrename reaches, else one — or none if it isn't a capability call. `args` are the arguments AS EVALUATED (what the\ndebugger's beforeCall already has).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:42.442Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:42.442Z"}
{"id":"c53f6634-551a-42f6-91e9-5dcfffe63721","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"f36424a867643226","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/capability-calls.ts","baseline":{"blob":"0ccde457526fd19ddce0248a4aae3ea6088823cc","start":5334,"end":5564},"shape":{"type":"Return","atoms":["return","effectiveDisposition","(","policy",",","hit",".","capability",",","hit",".","resource",",","hit",".","dangerous",",","{","\"","trigger","\"",":","\"","you","\"","}",")","===","\"","review","\"","&&","givenResult","(","policy",",","{","\"","trigger","\"",":","\"","you","\"",",","\"","capability","\"",":","hit",".","capability",",","\"","resource","\"",":","hit",".","resource","}",")","===","undefined"]},"context":{"before":"9ffa8a5c3a60ac2a#1","after":"e14ea72192523cd0"}},"payload":{"text":"A call a rule gives the result of (RUNNING.md, *A call's result*) never happens: the debugger's stand-in returns it\ninstead. (stops are armed only in runs someone is watching: `you`'s)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:40.360Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:40.360Z"}
{"id":"d47b4657-fc7c-4a6e-ab42-69d42beb8435","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"e14ea72192523cd0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/capability-calls.ts","baseline":{"blob":"926cd5e212f75cdb1e8fca4748b874a269f9a75c","start":5762,"end":6403},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","capabilityBreakLines","(","sourceFile",":","ts",".","SourceFile",",","policy",":","Policy",")",":","number","[]","{","const","lines","=","new","Set","<","number",">","(",")",";","(","function","visit","(","node",":","ts",".","Node",")",":","void","{","if","(","ts",".","isCallExpression","(","node",")",")","{","for","(","const","hit","of","classifyCall","(","node",",","[","]",")",")","{","const","argNode","=","node",".","arguments","[","hit",".","argIndex","]",";","const","resource","=","argNode","!==","undefined","&&","ts",".","isStringLiteralLike","(","argNode",")","?","argNode",".","text",":","\"","","\"",";","if","(","shouldBreak","(","policy",",","{","...","hit",",","\"","resource","\"",":","resource","}",")",")","{","lines",".","add","(","sourceFile",".","getLineAndCharacterOfPosition","(","node",".","getStart","(","sourceFile",")",")",".","line","+","1",")",";","}","}","}","node",".","forEachChild","(","visit",")",";","}",")","(","sourceFile",")",";","return","[","...","lines","]",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"85b27560343408eb"}},"payload":{"text":"The 1-based source lines a debugger should pre-arm as capability breakpoints under `policy` — every capability\ncall the policy would NOT let pass. The decision is STATIC (the resource is the literal argument when there is\none, else empty → an undecided dangerous call still breaks), because a debugger arms breakpoints at line\ngranularity BEFORE the run; the concrete runtime resource is then visible in the Variables pane at the stop.\nA debug worker adds these alongside the user's breakpoints, so a gated call hard-stops at its line with the\ndebugger's normal step / step-back.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:39.273Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:39.273Z"}
{"id":"e14e0ac4-83a6-40d9-8748-40d62bd9d008","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6cb9b46e8d2e9fab","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/capability-calls.ts","baseline":{"blob":"05bb5b88faef693c1f093213b402ae94597d65c5","start":0,"end":62},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Policy","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/util/silo/policy","\""]},"context":{"after":"24c06b64a7cd5152"}},"payload":{"text":"Capability breakpoints — the DECOUPLED decision layer between the capability policy and a debugger. A debugger\nthat runs the program (tsval's stepping VM today; an almostnode \"production\" adapter later) calls this at its\nhost-call boundary — the same `beforeCall` seam the canary uses — to answer ONE question: does the policy\nrequire a hard stop here? If so, the debugger pauses at that line (native VS Code debug UI); the user inspects,\nsteps (back, under tsval), and decides.\n\nKept free of any debugger/vscode dependency (only `typescript` for the AST node shape + silo's policy layer,\n`@brianjenkins94/util/silo/policy`) so it can be consumed from either the tsval debug worker or an almostnode adapter without coupling\nto either — the point of building it standalone first.\n\nClassification is AST-based (callee name → capability, a fixed argument as the resource), NOT the canary's\ntagged-stand-in trick: a debugger runs the program's REAL (or almostnode-shimmed) capabilities, not the canary's\nmocks, so there are no tags to read — the call node is what we have. (Aliasing like `const f = fetch` isn't\ncaught here, unlike the canary; a later refinement can resolve it.)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:50.816Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:50.816Z"}
{"id":"f975ba9a-d864-4a69-9815-e5ed9b5856c2","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"85b27560343408eb","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/capability-calls.ts","baseline":{"blob":"459334d7ab880df17cf0a4a9339bb44f25fcb6bd","start":4866,"end":5175},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","shouldBreak","(","policy",":","Policy",",","hit",":","CapabilityHit",")",":","boolean","{","return","effectiveDisposition","(","policy",",","hit",".","capability",",","hit",".","resource",",","hit",".","dangerous",",","{","\"","trigger","\"",":","\"","you","\"","}",")","===","\"","review","\"","&&","givenResult","(","policy",",","{","\"","trigger","\"",":","\"","you","\"",",","\"","capability","\"",":","hit",".","capability",",","\"","resource","\"",":","hit",".","resource","}",")","===","undefined",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"5c3d0596fdedba4b","after":"e14ea72192523cd0"}},"payload":{"text":"Does the policy require a hard stop at this capability hit? Break on an undecided dangerous call (`review`), so the\ndebugger pauses for every capability the user hasn't decided, firewall-style. A decided one passes: `allow` runs it,\n`skip` goes past it, `deny` fails it (EACCES) — a *Deny always* doesn't ask again (and non-dangerous, undecided,\npasses straight through).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:41.369Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:41.369Z"}
{"id":"f9fa3495-ba7e-4336-b6e3-6e3af2c35a97","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b692167e069946ac","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/capability-calls.ts","baseline":{"blob":"48fbfb9679d66f95f767bd281417ac7d3ffcb0bc","start":2095,"end":2199},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","IDENTIFIER_MATCHERS",":","Record","<","string",",","Matcher","[]",">","=","{","\"","fetch","\"",":","[","{","\"","capability","\"",":","\"","net","\"",",","\"","arg","\"",":","0","}","]","}"]},"context":{"before":"a6ceb63a7acca669","after":"2b71b92d456b876a"}},"payload":{"text":"Bare-identifier callees (`fetch(...)`) and the fido/http verb surface → net.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:47.561Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:58:47.561Z"}
